s, Feb. 7 to 10, Wang Renzhong there; a night with Zhou Enlai before Shanghai, three talks with Mao there; the Secretariat Apr. 9, 11 and 12; a meeting at Mao''s Apr. 22). Made public: 1967 ([[w.lin-biao-wenxuan-2]]). To check: [[w.gaoju-mao-zedong-sixiang]], 21 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-maos-last-revolution]], 38 n.25); [[w.nianyi-da-dongluande-niandai]], 10–12 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-origins-of-the-cultural]], III, 459 n.158a); Kang Sheng, speech of May 5–6, 1966 (part), and a later speech of Chen Boda, in [[w.lin-biao-wenxuan-2]], xia, 264–72 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-origins-of-the-cultural]], III, 459 n.158b); Lin Mohan 林默涵, 〈「文革」前的幾場文藝風波〉, in [[w.huishou-wenge-2-vols]], I, 265–266 (cited by [[w.pu-weihua-zalan-jiu-shijie]], 62 n.83). Names: Kang Sheng, Peng Zhen, Luo Ruiqing, Lu Dingyi. Check: the day of Zhang Chunqiao''s briefing. Check: the afternoon of May 6 ([[w.macfarquhar-origins-of-the-cultural]], III, 459); the briefing, which this entry carried, is now an entry of its own, [[cal.1966-05-06.china-leadership-2]]. Check: whether [[w.lin-biao-wenxuan-2]] (1967), a Red Guard compilation, on which the year rests, was printed for internal circulation; if so, Made public is the year of the next work cited.'
