     c: 'Peking, the enlarged Politburo session on Lu Dingyi''s self-criticism. On each chair a copy of a note in Lin Biao''s hand, dated May 14: Ye Qun a virgin at their marriage and faithful since; Yan Weibing''s letters nothing but rumor. Lu denies knowing of his wife''s letters; Lin threatens to kill him. The copies withdrawn at day''s end.'
-    n: '[[w.macfarquhar-maos-last-revolution]], 35; [[w.macfarquhar-origins-of-the-cultural]], III, 459 (the note on each seat; Lin Biao will not accept Lu Dingyi''s plea that he knew nothing of his wife''s letter); [[w.yang-jisheng-tiandi-fanfu]], I, 146, 148 (the note of Lin Biao, dated May 14, laid on each desk before the first plenary session of May 20; at the meeting Lu Dingyi, in his self-criticism, says he did not know of Yan Weibing''s letters and cannot speak falsely at the Politburo; Lin Biao presses how a husband could not know); [[w.teiwes-tragedy-of-lin-biao]], 15 (Lin circulates a letter that Ye Qun was a virgin at their marriage, against the anonymous charges of Lu Dingyi''s wife, and at the meeting attacks Lu: "I''d love to shoot you"); [[w.pu-weihua-zalan-jiu-shijie]], 88–89 (Lin Biao''s note, dated May 14, given out before Lu Dingyi''s self-criticism at the afternoon session of May 19: Ye Qun pure at their marriage and faithful since; she never loved Wang Shiwei; their children theirs; Yan Weibing''s letters all fabrications; Lu: he has the pen alone, is sixty-one and ill, could he make a coup; he knew nothing of the letters, his letter of Apr. 18 already said so; Lin, pounding the table, abuses him). Made public: 1967 ([[w.zhan-bao]], Jan. 18, 1967). To check: [[w.han-789-jizhongying]], 12–30 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-maos-last-revolution]], 35 n.16); [[w.nianyi-da-dongluande-niandai]], 19 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-maos-last-revolution]], 35 n.17); [[w.zhan-bao]], Jan. 18, 1967 (cited by [[w.macfarquhar-origins-of-the-cultural]], III, 459 n.162b); Chen Qingquan 陳清泉 and Song Guangwei 宋廣渭, *Lu Dingyi zhuan* 《陸定一傳》 (Zhonggong dangshi chubanshe 中共黨史出版社, 1999), 501 (cited by [[w.yang-jisheng-tiandi-fanfu]], I, 146 n.40); [[w.li-wang-li-fansi-lu]], the 2008 Beixing ed. 香港北星出版社 as Yang cites it, 24 (cited by [[w.yang-jisheng-tiandi-fanfu]], I, 148 n.46). Names: Lin Biao, Ye Qun, Lu Dingyi. Check: MacFarquhar (35) dates the note May 14 and the session by it.'
