     place: peking
     thread: china-leadership
     c: 'Ye Jianying 葉劍英 receives delegates of teachers and students of thirteen Peking art academies, and speaks. Of Lin Biao 林彪: Mao has chosen his first successor; Lin has rich experience of revolutionary struggle, is a great statesman and strategist, and will, in health better than any of ours, follow Mao for twenty or thirty years. Of the Red Guards: they have set up an "immortal merit"; Peking had over ten thousand "black households," and the Red Guards'' sweep, whatever the law, solved an old hard problem; it may break a little policy, but the greater gain is to clear away bad men and "the rubbish of our society."'
